{
  "concept": "Bucket sort distributes numbers in the half-open interval [0,1) into buckets by their first decimal digit, keeps each bucket list sorted, and then concatenates the buckets in order to produce the sorted sequence.",
  "figureType": "diagram",
  "elements": [
    "Panel label '(a)' beneath the input array",
    "Panel label '(b)' beneath the bucket array and linked lists",
    "italic header 'A' above the input array",
    "vertical gray input array A with 10 cells",
    "row indices 1 through 10 to the left of A",
    "A[1] value .78",
    "A[2] value .17",
    "A[3] value .39",
    "A[4] value .26",
    "A[5] value .72",
    "A[6] value .94",
    "A[7] value .21",
    "A[8] value .12",
    "A[9] value .23",
    "A[10] value .68",
    "italic header 'B' above the bucket array",
    "vertical gray bucket array B with 10 cells indexed 0 through 9",
    "bucket index labels 0 through 9 to the left of B",
    "empty bucket B[0] with diagonal null slash",
    "bucket B[1] head pointer arrow",
    "linked-list node .12 in bucket 1 with value field and pointer field",
    "pointer arrow from .12 node to .17 node",
    "linked-list node .17 in bucket 1 with terminating diagonal null slash",
    "bucket B[2] head pointer arrow",
    "linked-list node .21 in bucket 2 with value field and pointer field",
    "pointer arrow from .21 node to .23 node",
    "linked-list node .23 in bucket 2 with value field and pointer field",
    "pointer arrow from .23 node to .26 node",
    "linked-list node .26 in bucket 2 with terminating diagonal null slash",
    "bucket B[3] head pointer arrow",
    "linked-list node .39 in bucket 3 with terminating diagonal null slash",
    "empty bucket B[4] with diagonal null slash",
    "empty bucket B[5] with diagonal null slash",
    "bucket B[6] head pointer arrow",
    "linked-list node .68 in bucket 6 with terminating diagonal null slash",
    "bucket B[7] head pointer arrow",
    "linked-list node .72 in bucket 7 with value field and pointer field",
    "pointer arrow from .72 node to .78 node",
    "linked-list node .78 in bucket 7 with terminating diagonal null slash",
    "empty bucket B[8] with diagonal null slash",
    "bucket B[9] head pointer arrow",
    "linked-list node .94 in bucket 9 with terminating diagonal null slash",
    "dynamic highlight around the currently processed A cell",
    "dynamic highlight around the selected bucket B[i]",
    "dynamic annotation showing the computed interval [i/10, (i+1)/10)",
    "dynamic highlight around nodes compared during sorted insertion",
    "dynamic outline or glow around a newly inserted list node",
    "optional derived output row showing bucket lists concatenated from B[0] through B[9]"
  ],
  "interactions": [
    {
      "id": "bucketSortCode",
      "type": "code_editor",
      "label": "Bucket sort distribution code",
      "entry_point": "bucketSort(A)",
      "api": [
        {
          "op": "len(A)",
          "does": "return the number of input values in A"
        },
        {
          "op": "readA(i)",
          "does": "read A[i] and highlight that input cell in panel (a)"
        },
        {
          "op": "head(k)",
          "does": "return the first node in bucket B[k] and highlight bucket k and its half-open interval [k/10, (k+1)/10)"
        },
        {
          "op": "next(node)",
          "does": "return the next node in the linked list, or null at the end"
        },
        {
          "op": "lessValue(node, x)",
          "does": "true when node.value < x, highlighting the comparison used to keep the bucket sorted"
        },
        {
          "op": "insertAfter(k, prevNode, x)",
          "does": "create a new linked-list node holding x in bucket k after prevNode; if prevNode is null, insert at the head"
        },
        {
          "op": "note(message)",
          "does": "show a short explanatory annotation in the diagram"
        }
      ],
      "frame": "Each recorded step shows the whole input array A, all ten buckets B, the current A cell, the computed bucket index and interval, any linked-list comparisons, and the pointer update that inserts the new node.",
      "input": {
        "label": "Initial array values in [0,1)",
        "default": ".78, .17, .39, .26, .72, .94, .21, .12, .23, .68"
      },
      "sample_code": "function bucketSort(A) {\n  function bucketIndex(x) {\n    return Math.floor(10 * x);\n  }\n\n  function insertSorted(k, x) {\n    let prev = null;\n    let cur = head(k);\n    while (cur !== null && lessValue(cur, x)) {\n      prev = cur;\n      cur = next(cur);\n    }\n    insertAfter(k, prev, x);\n  }\n\n  for (let i = 0; i < len(A); i++) {\n    const x = readA(i);\n    const k = bucketIndex(x);\n    if (k < 0 || k >= 10) {\n      note('x = ' + x + ' is outside the bucket-sort assumption [0, 1)');\n    } else {\n      note(x + ' goes to bucket ' + k + ' because it lies in [' + (k/10) + ', ' + ((k+1)/10) + ')');\n      insertSorted(k, x);\n    }\n  }\n}",
      "buggy_code": "function bucketSort(A) {\n  function bucketIndex(x) {\n    return Math.round(10 * x); // BUG: rounding uses the nearest bucket, not the half-open interval floor rule\n  }\n\n  function insertSorted(k, x) {\n    let prev = null;\n    let cur = head(k);\n    while (cur !== null && lessValue(cur, x)) {\n      prev = cur;\n      cur = next(cur);\n    }\n    insertAfter(k, prev, x);\n  }\n\n  for (let i = 0; i < len(A); i++) {\n    const x = readA(i);\n    const k = bucketIndex(x);\n    if (k < 0 || k >= 10) {\n      note('out of range');\n    } else {\n      insertSorted(k, x);\n    }\n  }\n}",
      "success_check": "Every input value x satisfies 0 <= x < 1, appears exactly once in bucket floor(10*x), each bucket's linked list is in increasing order, and concatenating buckets B[0] through B[9] gives a globally sorted sequence.",
      "teaches": "The learner sees that floor(10*x) chooses the bucket by half-open decimal interval, and that sorted insertion inside each linked list is what makes simple left-to-right bucket concatenation produce the sorted output."
    }
  ],
  "demo_steps": [
    {
      "title": "Start with the unsorted input",
      "narration": "Panel (a) contains the original ten fractional values. The goal is not to compare every value with every other value, but to send each value to the bucket matching its first decimal digit.",
      "state": {}
    },
    {
      "title": "Compute the bucket index",
      "narration": "Step through the replay: when .78 is read, floor(10·.78)=7, so bucket B[7] and the interval [0.7,0.8) are highlighted. Values such as .12 and .17 both land in B[1] because both lie in [0.1,0.2).",
      "state": {}
    },
    {
      "title": "Insert into a sorted linked list",
      "narration": "As more values arrive, the code compares within only the selected bucket and inserts the new node in increasing order. Bucket B[2], for example, becomes .21 → .23 → .26 rather than just preserving input order.",
      "state": {}
    },
    {
      "title": "Test the half-open boundary rule",
      "narration": "Edit the input to try values near 0 and 1, such as .00, .099, .10, .94, and .999. The diagram flags that .94 belongs in bucket 9, while 1.0 would be outside the assumed interval [0,1).",
      "state": {}
    },
    {
      "title": "Concatenate the buckets",
      "narration": "After distribution, reading the nonempty buckets from B[0] to B[9] gives .12, .17, .21, .23, .26, .39, .68, .72, .78, .94. The buckets are ordered by interval, and each list is already sorted internally.",
      "state": {}
    }
  ],
  "keyInsight": "Bucket sort works here because floor(10x) partitions [0,1) into ordered half-open intervals, so only local sorting inside each bucket is needed before concatenation.",
  "reconstructionNotes": "Recreate the textbook layout as two side-by-side panels on a white background with light gray rectangular cells, black outlines, black arrows, and serif math-style labels. Panel (a) is a narrow vertical array A on the left with indices 1–10 and the listed decimal values. Panel (b) is a vertical bucket array B near the center with indices 0–9; nonempty buckets point right to horizontally arranged two-field linked-list nodes, and empty buckets show a diagonal slash. Keep each chain visually increasing from left to right. During replay, use a warm highlight for the current A cell, a blue highlight for the selected bucket and its interval annotation, and a green outline for newly inserted nodes; show boundary warnings in red only when an input is outside [0,1)."
}

